    ('july-05', '[{"key":"quick-reaction","title_en":"Your first reaction","title_ja":"最初の反応","description_en":"A situation where your first reaction changed after you learned more.","description_ja":"詳しく知るうちに、最初の反応が変わった出来事","speaking_prompt_en":"Speak for 60–90 seconds about a situation where your first reaction changed after you learned more. Give one concrete example and explain why it matters to you.","speaking_prompt_ja":"詳しく知るうちに、最初の反応が変わった出来事について60〜90秒で話してください。具体例を1つ挙げ、自分にとってなぜ大切かも説明しましょう。","essay_prompt_en":"Write 100–180 words about a situation where your first reaction changed after you learned more. Give a clear reason, one supporting example and a final takeaway.","essay_prompt_ja":"詳しく知るうちに、最初の反応が変わった出来事について100〜180語で書いてください。理由・具体例・最後のまとめを入れましょう。","challenge":"Core","phrases":["At first, I thought …","Then I realised …","Now I feel …"],"vocabulary":["reaction","impression","realise","perspective"]},{"key":"difficult-choice","title_en":"A difficult everyday choice","title_ja":"日常の迷う選択","description_en":"A recent choice between two reasonable options and how you decided.","description_ja":"どちらも悪くない2つの選択肢から、最近1つを選んだ経験","speaking_prompt_en":"Speak for 60–90 seconds about a recent choice between two reasonable options and how you decided. Give one concrete example and explain why it matters to you.","speaking_prompt_ja":"どちらも悪くない2つの選択肢から、最近1つを選んだ経験について60〜90秒で話してください。具体例を1つ挙げ、自分にとってなぜ大切かも説明しましょう。","essay_prompt_en":"Write 100–180 words about a recent choice between two reasonable options and how you decided. Give a clear reason, one supporting example and a final takeaway.","essay_prompt_ja":"どちらも悪くない2つの選択肢から、最近1つを選んだ経験について100〜180語で書いてください。理由・具体例・最後のまとめを入れましょう。","challenge":"Core","phrases":["I wasn’t sure whether to …","I decided on …","The main reason was …"],"vocabulary":["option","advantage","drawback","decision"]},{"key":"thinking-time","title_en":"Asking for time","title_ja":"考える時間をもらう","description_en":"Why taking time before answering can lead to a better decision.","description_ja":"返事の前に考える時間を取ると、より良い判断につながる理由","speaking_prompt_en":"Speak for 60–90 seconds about why taking time before answering can lead to a better decision. Give one concrete example and explain why it matters to you.","speaking_prompt_ja":"返事の前に考える時間を取ると、より良い判断につながる理由について60〜90秒で話してください。具体例を1つ挙げ、自分にとってなぜ大切かも説明しましょう。","essay_prompt_en":"Write 100–180 words about why taking time before answering can lead to a better decision. Give a clear reason, one supporting example and a final takeaway.","essay_prompt_ja":"返事の前に考える時間を取ると、より良い判断につながる理由について100〜180語で書いてください。理由・具体例・最後のまとめを入れましょう。","challenge":"Stretch","phrases":["Let me think about it.","I’m not ready to decide yet.","I’ll get back to you."],"vocabulary":["consider","pressure","deadline","response"]}]'::jsonb),
    ('july-06', '[{"key":"natural-conversation","title_en":"A smoother conversation","title_ja":"会話をなめらかにする","description_en":"What helps an English conversation sound connected rather than word by word.","description_ja":"英語の会話を単語ごとではなく、なめらかに聞こえさせる工夫","speaking_prompt_en":"Speak for 60–90 seconds about what helps an English conversation sound connected rather than word by word. Give one concrete example and explain why it matters to you.","speaking_prompt_ja":"英語の会話を単語ごとではなく、なめらかに聞こえさせる工夫について60〜90秒で話してください。具体例を1つ挙げ、自分にとってなぜ大切かも説明しましょう。","essay_prompt_en":"Write 100–180 words about what helps an English conversation sound connected rather than word by word. Give a clear reason, one supporting example and a final takeaway.","essay_prompt_ja":"英語の会話を単語ごとではなく、なめらかに聞こえさせる工夫について100〜180語で書いてください。理由・具体例・最後のまとめを入れましょう。","challenge":"Core","phrases":["What do you mean?","That makes sense.","Go on."],"vocabulary":["rhythm","connected speech","pause","intonation"]},{"key":"keeping-talking","title_en":"Keeping a conversation going","title_ja":"会話を続けるコツ","description_en":"Questions and reactions you use to keep a friendly conversation moving.","description_ja":"親しい会話を止めずに続けるための質問や反応","speaking_prompt_en":"Speak for 60–90 seconds about questions and reactions you use to keep a friendly conversation moving. Give one concrete example and explain why it matters to you.","speaking_prompt_ja":"親しい会話を止めずに続けるための質問や反応について60〜90秒で話してください。具体例を1つ挙げ、自分にとってなぜ大切かも説明しましょう。","essay_prompt_en":"Write 100–180 words about questions and reactions you use to keep a friendly conversation moving. Give a clear reason, one supporting example and a final takeaway.","essay_prompt_ja":"親しい会話を止めずに続けるための質問や反応について100〜180語で書いてください。理由・具体例・最後のまとめを入れましょう。","challenge":"Core","phrases":["How about you?","Really? What happened?","That sounds …"],"vocabulary":["follow-up","interest","response","conversation"]},{"key":"clarifying-meaning","title_en":"Checking the meaning","title_ja":"意味を確認する","description_en":"A time you needed to clarify someone’s meaning before responding.","description_ja":"返事をする前に、相手の意味を確認する必要があった場面","speaking_prompt_en":"Speak for 60–90 seconds about a time you needed to clarify someone’s meaning before responding. Give one concrete example and explain why it matters to you.","speaking_prompt_ja":"返事をする前に、相手の意味を確認する必要があった場面について60〜90秒で話してください。具体例を1つ挙げ、自分にとってなぜ大切かも説明しましょう。","essay_prompt_en":"Write 100–180 words about a time you needed to clarify someone’s meaning before responding. Give a clear reason, one supporting example and a final takeaway.","essay_prompt_ja":"返事をする前に、相手の意味を確認する必要があった場面について100〜180語で書いてください。理由・具体例・最後のまとめを入れましょう。","challenge":"Stretch","phrases":["Do you mean …?","So, are you saying …?","Let me make sure I understand."],"vocabulary":["clarify","intention","assumption","confirm"]}]'::jsonb),
    ('july-07', '[{"key":"thoughtful-gift","title_en":"A thoughtful gift","title_ja":"気持ちのこもった贈り物","description_en":"Something you bought or brought for another person and why you chose it.","description_ja":"誰かのために買ったり持っていったりした物と、それを選んだ理由","speaking_prompt_en":"Speak for 60–90 seconds about something you bought or brought for another person and why you chose it. Give one concrete example and explain why it matters to you.","speaking_prompt_ja":"誰かのために買ったり持っていったりした物と、それを選んだ理由について60〜90秒で話してください。具体例を1つ挙げ、自分にとってなぜ大切かも説明しましょう。","essay_prompt_en":"Write 100–180 words about something you bought or brought for another person and why you chose it. Give a clear reason, one supporting example and a final takeaway.","essay_prompt_ja":"誰かのために買ったり持っていったりした物と、それを選んだ理由について100〜180語で書いてください。理由・具体例・最後のまとめを入れましょう。","challenge":"Core","phrases":["I bought this for …","I brought you …","I thought you might like it."],"vocabulary":["gift","souvenir","thoughtful","choose"]},{"key":"helping-someone","title_en":"Doing something for someone","title_ja":"人のためにしたこと","description_en":"A practical thing you did on someone’s behalf.","description_ja":"誰かの代わりに、または誰かのためにした実用的なこと","speaking_prompt_en":"Speak for 60–90 seconds about a practical thing you did on someone’s behalf. Give one concrete example and explain why it matters to you.","speaking_prompt_ja":"誰かの代わりに、または誰かのためにした実用的なことについて60〜90秒で話してください。具体例を1つ挙げ、自分にとってなぜ大切かも説明しましょう。","essay_prompt_en":"Write 100–180 words about a practical thing you did on someone’s behalf. Give a clear reason, one supporting example and a final takeaway.","essay_prompt_ja":"誰かの代わりに、または誰かのためにした実用的なことについて100〜180語で書いてください。理由・具体例・最後のまとめを入れましょう。","challenge":"Core","phrases":["I did it for …","Let me take care of it.","I was happy to help."],"vocabulary":["behalf","favour","responsibility","support"]},{"key":"bring-or-buy","title_en":"Planning what to bring","title_ja":"持ち物を考える","description_en":"How you decide what to bring and what to buy for a visit or event.","description_ja":"訪問やイベントで、持参する物と買う物をどう決めるか","speaking_prompt_en":"Speak for 60–90 seconds about how you decide what to bring and what to buy for a visit or event. Give one concrete example and explain why it matters to you.","speaking_prompt_ja":"訪問やイベントで、持参する物と買う物をどう決めるかについて60〜90秒で話してください。具体例を1つ挙げ、自分にとってなぜ大切かも説明しましょう。","essay_prompt_en":"Write 100–180 words about how you decide what to bring and what to buy for a visit or event. Give a clear reason, one supporting example and a final takeaway.","essay_prompt_ja":"訪問やイベントで、持参する物と買う物をどう決めるかについて100〜180語で書いてください。理由・具体例・最後のまとめを入れましょう。","challenge":"Stretch","phrases":["I’ll bring …","We need to buy …","Do you already have …?"],"vocabulary":["supplies","prepare","purchase","occasion"]}]'::jsonb),
    ('july-11', '[{"key":"staying-connected","title_en":"Staying connected","title_ja":"つながりを保つ","description_en":"How technology helps you stay connected with people who live far away.","description_ja":"遠くに住む人とのつながりを、テクノロジーがどう支えるか","speaking_prompt_en":"Speak for 60–90 seconds about how technology helps you stay connected with people who live far away. Give one concrete example and explain why it matters to you.","speaking_prompt_ja":"遠くに住む人とのつながりを、テクノロジーがどう支えるかについて60〜90秒で話してください。具体例を1つ挙げ、自分にとってなぜ大切かも説明しましょう。","essay_prompt_en":"Write 100–180 words about how technology helps you stay connected with people who live far away. Give a clear reason, one supporting example and a final takeaway.","essay_prompt_ja":"遠くに住む人とのつながりを、テクノロジーがどう支えるかについて100〜180語で書いてください。理由・具体例・最後のまとめを入れましょう。","challenge":"Core","phrases":["We keep in touch through …","It helps us stay connected.","We usually catch up …"],"vocabulary":["connection","video call","distance","regularly"]},{"key":"live-experience","title_en":"Live or recorded?","title_ja":"ライブか録画か","description_en":"Whether you prefer a live event or a recording and why.","description_ja":"イベントはライブと録画のどちらが好きか、その理由","speaking_prompt_en":"Speak for 60–90 seconds about whether you prefer a live event or a recording and why. Give one concrete example and explain why it matters to you.","speaking_prompt_ja":"イベントはライブと録画のどちらが好きか、その理由について60〜90秒で話してください。具体例を1つ挙げ、自分にとってなぜ大切かも説明しましょう。","essay_prompt_en":"Write 100–180 words about whether you prefer a live event or a recording and why. Give a clear reason, one supporting example and a final takeaway.","essay_prompt_ja":"イベントはライブと録画のどちらが好きか、その理由について100〜180語で書いてください。理由・具体例・最後のまとめを入れましょう。","challenge":"Core","phrases":["I’d rather watch it live.","A recording is convenient because …","The atmosphere is …"],"vocabulary":["broadcast","stream","audience","atmosphere"]},{"key":"notice-a-change","title_en":"A change you noticed","title_ja":"気づいた変化","description_en":"A small change you noticed late and what made you realise it.","description_ja":"少し遅れて気づいた小さな変化と、気づくきっかけ","speaking_prompt_en":"Speak for 60–90 seconds about a small change you noticed late and what made you realise it. Give one concrete example and explain why it matters to you.","speaking_prompt_ja":"少し遅れて気づいた小さな変化と、気づくきっかけについて60〜90秒で話してください。具体例を1つ挙げ、自分にとってなぜ大切かも説明しましょう。","essay_prompt_en":"Write 100–180 words about a small change you noticed late and what made you realise it. Give a clear reason, one supporting example and a final takeaway.","essay_prompt_ja":"少し遅れて気づいた小さな変化と、気づくきっかけについて100〜180語で書いてください。理由・具体例・最後のまとめを入れましょう。","challenge":"Stretch","phrases":["I noticed that …","I didn’t realise until …","Something seemed different."],"vocabulary":["notice","realise","detail","gradual"]}]'::jsonb),
    ('july-12', '[{"key":"learning-progress","title_en":"Progress so far","title_ja":"これまでの上達","description_en":"Something you have improved at and what helped you make progress.","description_ja":"上達したことと、進歩につながった方法","speaking_prompt_en":"Speak for 60–90 seconds about something you have improved at and what helped you make progress. Give one concrete example and explain why it matters to you.","speaking_prompt_ja":"上達したことと、進歩につながった方法について60〜90秒で話してください。具体例を1つ挙げ、自分にとってなぜ大切かも説明しましょう。","essay_prompt_en":"Write 100–180 words about something you have improved at and what helped you make progress. Give a clear reason, one supporting example and a final takeaway.","essay_prompt_ja":"上達したことと、進歩につながった方法について100〜180語で書いてください。理由・具体例・最後のまとめを入れましょう。","challenge":"Core","phrases":["I’ve improved …","I haven’t mastered it yet.","What has helped most is …"],"vocabulary":["progress","practice","achievement","yet"]},{"key":"past-experience","title_en":"An experience you had","title_ja":"これまでの経験","description_en":"A past experience that changed how you do something now.","description_ja":"今の行動を変えるきっかけになった過去の経験","speaking_prompt_en":"Speak for 60–90 seconds about a past experience that changed how you do something now. Give one concrete example and explain why it matters to you.","speaking_prompt_ja":"今の行動を変えるきっかけになった過去の経験について60〜90秒で話してください。具体例を1つ挙げ、自分にとってなぜ大切かも説明しましょう。","essay_prompt_en":"Write 100–180 words about a past experience that changed how you do something now. Give a clear reason, one supporting example and a final takeaway.","essay_prompt_ja":"今の行動を変えるきっかけになった過去の経験について100〜180語で書いてください。理由・具体例・最後のまとめを入れましょう。","challenge":"Core","phrases":["I had never … before.","After that, I …","It has changed …"],"vocabulary":["experience","lesson","previously","since"]},{"key":"not-yet","title_en":"A goal not reached yet","title_ja":"まだ達成していない目標","description_en":"A useful goal you have not achieved yet and your next step.","description_ja":"まだ達成していない実用的な目標と、次にすること","speaking_prompt_en":"Speak for 60–90 seconds about a useful goal you have not achieved yet and your next step. Give one concrete example and explain why it matters to you.","speaking_prompt_ja":"まだ達成していない実用的な目標と、次にすることについて60〜90秒で話してください。具体例を1つ挙げ、自分にとってなぜ大切かも説明しましょう。","essay_prompt_en":"Write 100–180 words about a useful goal you have not achieved yet and your next step. Give a clear reason, one supporting example and a final takeaway.","essay_prompt_ja":"まだ達成していない実用的な目標と、次にすることについて100〜180語で書いてください。理由・具体例・最後のまとめを入れましょう。","challenge":"Stretch","phrases":["I haven’t … yet.","I’ve already started …","My next step is …"],"vocabulary":["goal","milestone","already","plan"]}]'::jsonb),
    ('july-13', '[{"key":"possible-plan","title_en":"A possible plan","title_ja":"実現するかもしれない予定","description_en":"A plan that might happen and what needs to be decided first.","description_ja":"実現するかもしれない予定と、先に決める必要があること","speaking_prompt_en":"Speak for 60–90 seconds about a plan that might happen and what needs to be decided first. Give one concrete example and explain why it matters to you.","speaking_prompt_ja":"実現するかもしれない予定と、先に決める必要があることについて60〜90秒で話してください。具体例を1つ挙げ、自分にとってなぜ大切かも説明しましょう。","essay_prompt_en":"Write 100–180 words about a plan that might happen and what needs to be decided first. Give a clear reason, one supporting example and a final takeaway.","essay_prompt_ja":"実現するかもしれない予定と、先に決める必要があることについて100〜180語で書いてください。理由・具体例・最後のまとめを入れましょう。","challenge":"Core","phrases":["I might …","There’s a chance that …","It depends on …"],"vocabulary":["possibility","arrangement","confirm","condition"]},{"key":"best-time","title_en":"The best time of day","title_ja":"一番過ごしやすい時間帯","description_en":"Which part of the day suits you best for work, study or relaxation.","description_ja":"仕事・勉強・休憩に一番合う時間帯","speaking_prompt_en":"Speak for 60–90 seconds about which part of the day suits you best for work, study or relaxation. Give one concrete example and explain why it matters to you.","speaking_prompt_ja":"仕事・勉強・休憩に一番合う時間帯について60〜90秒で話してください。具体例を1つ挙げ、自分にとってなぜ大切かも説明しましょう。","essay_prompt_en":"Write 100–180 words about which part of the day suits you best for work, study or relaxation. Give a clear reason, one supporting example and a final takeaway.","essay_prompt_ja":"仕事・勉強・休憩に一番合う時間帯について100〜180語で書いてください。理由・具体例・最後のまとめを入れましょう。","challenge":"Core","phrases":["I’m most productive …","Around midday, …","Late at night, …"],"vocabulary":["morning","midday","evening","productive"]},{"key":"city-moment","title_en":"A moment in the city","title_ja":"街での出来事","description_en":"A small problem or discovery you experienced while moving around a city.","description_ja":"街を移動しているときに経験した、小さな問題や発見","speaking_prompt_en":"Speak for 60–90 seconds about a small problem or discovery you experienced while moving around a city. Give one concrete example and explain why it matters to you.","speaking_prompt_ja":"街を移動しているときに経験した、小さな問題や発見について60〜90秒で話してください。具体例を1つ挙げ、自分にとってなぜ大切かも説明しましょう。","essay_prompt_en":"Write 100–180 words about a small problem or discovery you experienced while moving around a city. Give a clear reason, one supporting example and a final takeaway.","essay_prompt_ja":"街を移動しているときに経験した、小さな問題や発見について100〜180語で書いてください。理由・具体例・最後のまとめを入れましょう。","challenge":"Stretch","phrases":["I had to rush back.","I was on my way to …","I suddenly realised …"],"vocabulary":["commute","entrance","crowded","direction"]}]'::jsonb),
    ('july-18', '[{"key":"missed-obligation","title_en":"A plan you missed","title_ja":"できなかった予定","description_en":"Something you were supposed to do but could not complete.","description_ja":"する予定だったのに、できなかったこと","speaking_prompt_en":"Speak for 60–90 seconds about something you were supposed to do but could not complete. Give one concrete example and explain why it matters to you.","speaking_prompt_ja":"する予定だったのに、できなかったことについて60〜90秒で話してください。具体例を1つ挙げ、自分にとってなぜ大切かも説明しましょう。","essay_prompt_en":"Write 100–180 words about something you were supposed to do but could not complete. Give a clear reason, one supporting example and a final takeaway.","essay_prompt_ja":"する予定だったのに、できなかったことについて100〜180語で書いてください。理由・具体例・最後のまとめを入れましょう。","challenge":"Core","phrases":["I was supposed to …","I couldn’t because …","I should have …"],"vocabulary":["obligation","deadline","explanation","reschedule"]},{"key":"asking-for-help","title_en":"Getting the right help","title_ja":"必要な助けを求める","description_en":"A situation where a helper or professional made a difficult moment easier.","description_ja":"困ったときに、専門家や周りの人の助けで楽になった場面","speaking_prompt_en":"Speak for 60–90 seconds about a situation where a helper or professional made a difficult moment easier. Give one concrete example and explain why it matters to you.","speaking_prompt_ja":"困ったときに、専門家や周りの人の助けで楽になった場面について60〜90秒で話してください。具体例を1つ挙げ、自分にとってなぜ大切かも説明しましょう。","essay_prompt_en":"Write 100–180 words about a situation where a helper or professional made a difficult moment easier. Give a clear reason, one supporting example and a final takeaway.","essay_prompt_ja":"困ったときに、専門家や周りの人の助けで楽になった場面について100〜180語で書いてください。理由・具体例・最後のまとめを入れましょう。","challenge":"Core","phrases":["Could you help me with …?","I need someone who can …","Thank you for stepping in."],"vocabulary":["assistant","emergency service","support","responsibility"]},{"key":"fire-safety","title_en":"Responding safely","title_ja":"安全に対応する","description_en":"What people should do first if they notice a fire or another emergency.","description_ja":"火災などの緊急事態に気づいたとき、最初にすべきこと","speaking_prompt_en":"Speak for 60–90 seconds about what people should do first if they notice a fire or another emergency. Give one concrete example and explain why it matters to you.","speaking_prompt_ja":"火災などの緊急事態に気づいたとき、最初にすべきことについて60〜90秒で話してください。具体例を1つ挙げ、自分にとってなぜ大切かも説明しましょう。","essay_prompt_en":"Write 100–180 words about what people should do first if they notice a fire or another emergency. Give a clear reason, one supporting example and a final takeaway.","essay_prompt_ja":"火災などの緊急事態に気づいたとき、最初にすべきことについて100〜180語で書いてください。理由・具体例・最後のまとめを入れましょう。","challenge":"Stretch","phrases":["The building is on fire.","We need to leave now.","Call the fire department."],"vocabulary":["evacuate","alarm","emergency exit","firefighter"]}]'::jsonb),
    ('july-19', '[{"key":"either-plan","title_en":"Two workable plans","title_ja":"どちらでもよい予定","description_en":"Two plans that would both work and how you would respond clearly.","description_ja":"どちらでも問題ない2つの予定と、分かりやすい返答","speaking_prompt_en":"Speak for 60–90 seconds about two plans that would both work and how you would respond clearly. Give one concrete example and explain why it matters to you.","speaking_prompt_ja":"どちらでも問題ない2つの予定と、分かりやすい返答について60〜90秒で話してください。具体例を1つ挙げ、自分にとってなぜ大切かも説明しましょう。","essay_prompt_en":"Write 100–180 words about two plans that would both work and how you would respond clearly. Give a clear reason, one supporting example and a final takeaway.","essay_prompt_ja":"どちらでも問題ない2つの予定と、分かりやすい返答について100〜180語で書いてください。理由・具体例・最後のまとめを入れましょう。","challenge":"Core","phrases":["Either one works for me.","Both options are fine.","I’m available on …"],"vocabulary":["either","both","option","available"]},{"key":"strong-preference","title_en":"What you would rather do","title_ja":"どちらかを選ぶなら","description_en":"A choice where you would clearly rather do one thing than the other.","description_ja":"2つの選択肢のうち、はっきり一方を選びたい場面","speaking_prompt_en":"Speak for 60–90 seconds about a choice where you would clearly rather do one thing than the other. Give one concrete example and explain why it matters to you.","speaking_prompt_ja":"2つの選択肢のうち、はっきり一方を選びたい場面について60〜90秒で話してください。具体例を1つ挙げ、自分にとってなぜ大切かも説明しましょう。","essay_prompt_en":"Write 100–180 words about a choice where you would clearly rather do one thing than the other. Give a clear reason, one supporting example and a final takeaway.","essay_prompt_ja":"2つの選択肢のうち、はっきり一方を選びたい場面について100〜180語で書いてください。理由・具体例・最後のまとめを入れましょう。","challenge":"Core","phrases":["I would rather …","I’d prefer to …","The reason is …"],"vocabulary":["rather","preference","convenient","priority"]},{"key":"neither-option","title_en":"When neither works","title_ja":"どちらも合わないとき","description_en":"How to respond politely when neither of two suggestions works for you.","description_ja":"2つの提案がどちらも合わないときの、丁寧な返し方","speaking_prompt_en":"Speak for 60–90 seconds about how to respond politely when neither of two suggestions works for you. Give one concrete example and explain why it matters to you.","speaking_prompt_ja":"2つの提案がどちらも合わないときの、丁寧な返し方について60〜90秒で話してください。具体例を1つ挙げ、自分にとってなぜ大切かも説明しましょう。","essay_prompt_en":"Write 100–180 words about how to respond politely when neither of two suggestions works for you. Give a clear reason, one supporting example and a final takeaway.","essay_prompt_ja":"2つの提案がどちらも合わないときの、丁寧な返し方について100〜180語で書いてください。理由・具体例・最後のまとめを入れましょう。","challenge":"Stretch","phrases":["Neither option works for me.","Could we consider …?","Would another day be possible?"],"vocabulary":["neither","alternative","conflict","suggestion"]}]'::jsonb),
    ('july-22', '[{"key":"meeting-time","title_en":"Finding a meeting time","title_ja":"会う時間を決める","description_en":"How you would arrange a meeting time that works for everyone.","description_ja":"全員に都合のよい会議時間を決める方法","speaking_prompt_en":"Speak for 60–90 seconds about how you would arrange a meeting time that works for everyone. Give one concrete example and explain why it matters to you.","speaking_prompt_ja":"全員に都合のよい会議時間を決める方法について60〜90秒で話してください。具体例を1つ挙げ、自分にとってなぜ大切かも説明しましょう。","essay_prompt_en":"Write 100–180 words about how you would arrange a meeting time that works for everyone. Give a clear reason, one supporting example and a final takeaway.","essay_prompt_ja":"全員に都合のよい会議時間を決める方法について100〜180語で書いてください。理由・具体例・最後のまとめを入れましょう。","challenge":"Core","phrases":["Would you be available …?","That time works for me.","Could we move it to …?"],"vocabulary":["availability","appointment","schedule","reschedule"]},{"key":"clear-answer","title_en":"A clear yes or no","title_ja":"分かりやすいYes・No","description_en":"Why clear answers matter when someone asks a negative question.","description_ja":"否定疑問文を聞かれたとき、明確に答えることが大切な理由","speaking_prompt_en":"Speak for 60–90 seconds about why clear answers matter when someone asks a negative question. Give one concrete example and explain why it matters to you.","speaking_prompt_ja":"否定疑問文を聞かれたとき、明確に答えることが大切な理由について60〜90秒で話してください。具体例を1つ挙げ、自分にとってなぜ大切かも説明しましょう。","essay_prompt_en":"Write 100–180 words about why clear answers matter when someone asks a negative question. Give a clear reason, one supporting example and a final takeaway.","essay_prompt_ja":"否定疑問文を聞かれたとき、明確に答えることが大切な理由について100〜180語で書いてください。理由・具体例・最後のまとめを入れましょう。","challenge":"Core","phrases":["Yes, I am.","No, I’m not.","To be clear, …"],"vocabulary":["negative question","confirm","confusion","direct"]},{"key":"flexible-choice","title_en":"Being flexible","title_ja":"柔軟に選ぶ","description_en":"A situation where either of two choices is genuinely fine for you.","description_ja":"2つの選択肢のどちらでも本当に問題ない場面","speaking_prompt_en":"Speak for 60–90 seconds about a situation where either of two choices is genuinely fine for you. Give one concrete example and explain why it matters to you.","speaking_prompt_ja":"2つの選択肢のどちらでも本当に問題ない場面について60〜90秒で話してください。具体例を1つ挙げ、自分にとってなぜ大切かも説明しましょう。","essay_prompt_en":"Write 100–180 words about a situation where either of two choices is genuinely fine for you. Give a clear reason, one supporting example and a final takeaway.","essay_prompt_ja":"2つの選択肢のどちらでも本当に問題ない場面について100〜180語で書いてください。理由・具体例・最後のまとめを入れましょう。","challenge":"Stretch","phrases":["Either is fine.","I don’t mind which one.","Whatever works best for you."],"vocabulary":["flexible","preference","arrangement","convenient"]}]'::jsonb),
    ('july-23', '[{"key":"under-weather","title_en":"Feeling under the weather","title_ja":"少し体調が悪いとき","description_en":"How you change your plans when you feel slightly unwell.","description_ja":"少し体調が悪いときに、予定をどう変更するか","speaking_prompt_en":"Speak for 60–90 seconds about how you change your plans when you feel slightly unwell. Give one concrete example and explain why it matters to you.","speaking_prompt_ja":"少し体調が悪いときに、予定をどう変更するかについて60〜90秒で話してください。具体例を1つ挙げ、自分にとってなぜ大切かも説明しましょう。","essay_prompt_en":"Write 100–180 words about how you change your plans when you feel slightly unwell. Give a clear reason, one supporting example and a final takeaway.","essay_prompt_ja":"少し体調が悪いときに、予定をどう変更するかについて100〜180語で書いてください。理由・具体例・最後のまとめを入れましょう。","challenge":"Core","phrases":["I’m feeling under the weather.","I might need to rest.","Can we do it another day?"],"vocabulary":["symptom","rest","recover","postpone"]},{"key":"future-invention","title_en":"A useful future invention","title_ja":"未来の便利な発明","description_en":"A Doraemon-style gadget that would solve a real everyday problem.","description_ja":"日常の困りごとを解決する、ドラえもんの道具のような発明","speaking_prompt_en":"Speak for 60–90 seconds about a Doraemon-style gadget that would solve a real everyday problem. Give one concrete example and explain why it matters to you.","speaking_prompt_ja":"日常の困りごとを解決する、ドラえもんの道具のような発明について60〜90秒で話してください。具体例を1つ挙げ、自分にとってなぜ大切かも説明しましょう。","essay_prompt_en":"Write 100–180 words about a Doraemon-style gadget that would solve a real everyday problem. Give a clear reason, one supporting example and a final takeaway.","essay_prompt_ja":"日常の困りごとを解決する、ドラえもんの道具のような発明について100〜180語で書いてください。理由・具体例・最後のまとめを入れましょう。","challenge":"Core","phrases":["It would allow people to …","I haven’t thought of a name yet.","It could be useful when …"],"vocabulary":["gadget","invention","convenient","imagine"]},{"key":"movement-habit","title_en":"An everyday movement habit","title_ja":"日常の動作習慣","description_en":"A healthy movement or exercise habit you 